story: You rented an HDB flat from Mr Tan Ah Kow under a 12-month tenancy agreement, from 3 Aug 2025 to 2 Aug 2026, and paid him a security deposit of $2,600 on signing (source E1 Clause 4, p.2). At handover on 15 Aug 2026, an inventory list was signed by both parties to record the condition of the furniture and fittings (source E1 Clause 6, p.3), and the agreement required you to hand back the premises clean and in good condition, fair wear and tear excepted (source E1 Clause 10, p.4). When you moved out, Mr Tan said everything was ok and all good, but two weeks later he said the sofa was scratched and refused to return your $2,600 deposit (source E2 shot 5).
summary: 500 I rented an HDB flat from the Respondent, Mr Tan Ah Kow, under a tenancy agreement for 12 months, from 3 Aug 2025 to 2 Aug 2026. I paid a security deposit of $2,600 on signing. The agreement says he must return the deposit within 14 days after I move out, minus any damage. On 15 Aug 2026 I moved out and handed over the flat. He checked and said everything was fine. Two weeks later he said the sofa was scratched and refused to return my deposit. I have my move-in photos, move-out video, and payme
